course: dictionary
lesson: 8395
title: Understanding rudeness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rudeness is behaviour or talk that is not polite and does not show respect. It can be interrupting, name-calling or ignoring someone. Rudeness is also the quality of being rude, as in the phrase «excuse my rudeness».
explain: Read the words around it to check. «Rudeness often costs friendships and invitations, even when you did not mean to be rude.» The clue is costs friendships, so rudeness can hurt people, even by accident.
explain: Not every strong action is rudeness. «A growl is a warning, not rudeness.» A dog growling to warn someone is giving a signal, not being disrespectful. Ask yourself: is this impolite or disrespectful? If not, it is not rudeness.
fact: Rudeness means behaviour that is not polite and does not show respect.
fact: Examples of rudeness include interrupting, name-calling, ignoring someone, and pushing in a queue.
fact: «Rudeness to adults comes in many forms: shouting at the coach, mocking an accent, muttering, slamming a door.»
fact: «Put up with rudeness» means accept it without complaining.
fact: Rudeness has no plural. You say «some rudeness», not «rudenesses».
exercise: «Rudeness often costs friendships and invitations, even when you did not mean to be rude.» What does rudeness mean here? | A kind gift | Being very clever at school | *Behaviour that is not polite and does not show respect | Telling a funny joke
exercise: «A growl is a warning, not rudeness.» Why is a growl not rudeness? | It means the dog is happy | It is always rude | It is a kind word | *It is a warning, not behaviour that disrespects someone
exercise: Which of these is an example of rudeness? | Waiting your turn in a queue | *Interrupting someone while they are talking | Saying please and thank you | Holding a door open
test: Mia says «please» and «thank you» at dinner. Is she showing rudeness? | Yes, because she speaks at dinner | Yes, because words are never rude | Yes, because she says thank you too often | *No, she is being polite and showing respect
test: Which action would count as rudeness in a queue? | *Pushing in front of others | Waiting patiently for your turn | Smiling at the person behind you | Saying excuse me to get past
exam: Which is the best reason a growl is not rudeness? | Growls are very loud | Dogs are always polite | Growling is a happy sound | *It is a warning, not an insult or a lack of respect
